# Versioning & GitHub release

Agents **decide and apply** the semver bump from the **scope of the change**. Do **not** ask patch vs minor vs major unless the scope is genuinely ambiguous.

**Override only when the user explicitly says so** — e.g. “no version bump”, “stay on 1.1.0”, “bump major”, “patch only”.

## When to bump

Bump **before** a release tag or when shipping work that will be released (merge to `main` + tag). Include version + changelog in the same commit/PR as the feature when release-bound.

Do **not** bump for WIP, docs-only, or CI-only changes unless releasing.

## Choose bump kind (agent decides)

| Kind | Use when |
|------|----------|
| **patch** | Bug fixes; refactors/tests/CI with no user-visible change; copy/a11y polish; performance; non-breaking Drift migrations |
| **minor** | New user-facing capability, screen, flow, or export option; meaningful UX addition; additive schema that unlocks new behavior |
| **major** | Breaking user impact — incompatible backup/import, removed feature or language, intentional data-model break users must act on |

When in doubt between patch and minor → **minor** if end users would notice new capability; else **patch**.

## Apply (in order)

1. `dart run tool/bump_version.dart <major\|minor\|patch>`
2. Prepend a `ChangelogEntry` in `lib/core/version/app_changelog.dart` for the new version — **en + fa**, end-user bullets from the actual changes
3. `./tool/ci_verify.sh` (must exit 0)
4. Commit version + changelog with the feature (or a dedicated release commit on `main`)

## Tag & GitHub Release (when user wants a release)

Only after green CI on `main`:

```bash
./tool/ci_verify.sh --tag vX.Y.Z   # X.Y.Z must match AppVersion.name
git tag vX.Y.Z && git push origin vX.Y.Z
```

CI on `v*` tags: Verify → Build APK → GitHub Release with `nasyad-vX.Y.Z.apk`.

## Tell the user (one line)

State the chosen bump, why (scope), new version, and whether a tag was pushed.
